# .NET / C# backend standards (mandatory)

Triggered by `**/*.cs` / `*.csproj` (see also always-on `skill-auto-router.mdc`). When writing, editing, reviewing, or refactoring any C# / .NET code (especially under `apps/backend/`), you MUST follow these project skills before and while changing code:

1. Read and apply [`.cursor/skills/dotnet-modular-monolith/SKILL.md`](../skills/dotnet-modular-monolith/SKILL.md) — dependency graph, Domain/Application/Infrastructure/Features, tenancy, outbox-in-TX, hosting pipeline, tests.
2. Read and apply [`.cursor/skills/dotnet-clean-code/SKILL.md`](../skills/dotnet-clean-code/SKILL.md) — Clean Code, SOLID, naming, Result vs exceptions, anti-God-services.
3. For new public names (commands, events, types, routes), also apply [`.cursor/skills/semantic-naming/SKILL.md`](../skills/semantic-naming/SKILL.md).

## Non-negotiable while coding

- Respect the project reference graph (SharedKernel → nobody; Platform ↛ Modules; Domain ↛ Infrastructure).
- Tenant only from validated JWT → `ICurrentTenant`; never trust client tenant headers in Production.
- Stage outbox in the same transaction as the write.
- Keep endpoints thin; put invariants in Domain/Application.
- Prefer `sealed` types, explicit records, narrow ports, one-verb handlers.
- Expected business failures → `Result` / domain codes; propagate `CancellationToken`; use `TimeProvider`.
- Prefer `using` + short type names for Contracts/ports; FQN only for collisions, one-offs, or string/meta (EF, NetArchTest, migrations).

## Before finishing a C# change

- [ ] Pre-PR checklists in both skills satisfied for the touched surface
- [ ] No new cross-module project reference or Domain→Infra leak
- [ ] Multi-tenant scoping correct for any new query/write
